{"id":"e118f18d4da6f655","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-handle-attaching.md","title":"Handle Attaching","display":"df-handle-attaching — Handle Attaching","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-handle-attaching","aliases":["58-df-handle-attaching","Handle Attaching"],"display":"df-handle-attaching — Handle Attaching","depends_on":["[[../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md]]","[[58-df-handle]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-handle-attaching"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-handle-attaching</span><span>Handle Attaching</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-handle-attaching — Handle Attaching"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca7fc3ab38a11801\" href=\"?note=ca7fc3ab38a11801\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md\">../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c8ba6230066eaf8b\" href=\"?note=c8ba6230066eaf8b\" title=\"58-df-handle\">58-df-handle</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-manifold with boundary)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h^k = D^k \\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\">\\(h^k = D^k \\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>-handle)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\phi:\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\to\\partial M\">\\(\\phi:\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\to\\partial M\\)</span> (attaching map)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N\">\\(N\\)</span> (result of the attachment)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Handle}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Handle}_S\\)</span> (handle predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c8ba6230066eaf8b\" href=\"?note=c8ba6230066eaf8b\" title=\"58-df-handle\">58-df-handle</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AttachedManifold}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{AttachedManifold}_S\\)</span> (typed handle-attachment predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"c8ba6230066eaf8b\" href=\"?note=c8ba6230066eaf8b\" title=\"58-df-handle\">58-df-handle</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HandleAttachment}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{HandleAttachment}_S\\)</span> (dimension- and index-explicit handle attachment predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\">\\(\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\">\\(\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\)</span> 使用内部有限函数向量载体，特别地 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(0)=\\varnothing\">\\(\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(0)=\\varnothing\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\phi\">\\(\\phi\\)</span> 的定义域不再借用未定义的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^{-1}\">\\(S^{-1}\\)</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}handle\\text{-}attaching} \\vdash \\mathrm{HandleAttachment}_S(N,M,h,\\phi,k,n)\\leftrightarrow n,k\\in\\omega\\land k\\leq n\\land\\mathrm{Handle}_S(h,k,n)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\phi)=\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\land\\mathrm{AttachedManifold}_S(N,M,h,\\phi)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}handle\\text{-}attaching} \\vdash \\mathrm{HandleAttachment}_S(N,M,h,\\phi,k,n)\\leftrightarrow n,k\\in\\omega\\land k\\leq n\\land\\mathrm{Handle}_S(h,k,n)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\phi)=\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\land\\mathrm{AttachedManifold}_S(N,M,h,\\phi)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle attaching uses the upstream typed manifold attachment, while the repaired wrapper records <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k,n\">\\(k,n\\)</span> as actual arguments and requires the attaching-map domain to match them.</li>\n<li>Handles: basic building blocks; 0-handle is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D^n\">\\(D^n\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-handle is dual <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D^0\">\\(D^0\\)</span></li>\n<li>Decomposition: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> built from 0-handle by attaching <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>-handles for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"1 \\leq k \\leq n\">\\(1 \\leq k \\leq n\\)</span></li>\n<li>Surgery: handle attachment changes homology; framed by attaching sphere</li>\n<li>Index and homotopy quotient effects are downstream properties.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Milnor, Morse Theory</li>\n<li>Gompf and Stipsicz, 4-Manifolds and Kirby Calculus</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca7fc3ab38a11801","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-handle","status":"resolved","id":"c8ba6230066eaf8b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-handle]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-handle","status":"resolved","id":"c8ba6230066eaf8b","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Handle}_S$ (handle predicate, see [[58-df-handle]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-handle","status":"resolved","id":"c8ba6230066eaf8b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{AttachedManifold}_S$ (typed handle-attachment predicate, see [[58-df-handle]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"h^k = D^k \\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false},{"tex":"\\phi:\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\to\\partial M","display":false},{"tex":"N","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Handle}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AttachedManifold}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HandleAttachment}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(0)=\\varnothing","display":false},{"tex":"\\phi","display":false},{"tex":"S^{-1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}handle\\text{-}attaching} \\vdash \\mathrm{HandleAttachment}_S(N,M,h,\\phi,k,n)\\leftrightarrow n,k\\in\\omega\\land k\\leq n\\land\\mathrm{Handle}_S(h,k,n)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\phi)=\\mathrm{DiskBoundary}_S(k)\\times\\mathrm{ClosedUnitDisk}_S(n-k)\\land\\mathrm{AttachedManifold}_S(N,M,h,\\phi)","display":true},{"tex":"k,n","display":false},{"tex":"D^n","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"D^0","display":false},{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false},{"tex":"1 \\leq k \\leq n","display":false}],"bytes":1972,"backlinks":[{"id":"580cc04d629fcdb8","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt